Z||000000||XDrewX||08-12-2001||11:28 PM||||I am laying down the plans for my modifications, which i hope to start in October.<P>My plan is to find a 97 to 99 pontiac grand prix GTP, and basically swap everything interior, including entire dashboard with guages, electrical stuff, etc. and engine/transmission into my 87 GT. (i know seats wont fit)<P>I wont be tranfering the air bags, so i need to figure out how to keep that from becoming a problem with the computer.<P>I know some of you have done the 3800 swap, but has anyone tried this or is there a big problem i am not seeing ?????||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||08-13-2001||12:04 AM||||Hm. I'd think I'd just keep the GTP.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  One of my friends just bought one a few months ago ('97) for $14k.  Really fast, at least 0-60 anyway.  Too bad it's FWD though.  And I wouldn't be surprised if it could out-handle my GT in the corners.  For a big car, it's awesome in the turns.||||reg||1
