Z||000006||Jncomutt||08-13-2001||03:08 PM||||I think my 84 is an exception to the handling ablility.  Given I've never owned anyother car besides my 2 fieros, it doesn't seem to handle as well as everyone says it should.  I notice when I go around corners, the front end loves to slide and not follow where I'm trying ta put the car.  Is this because my cars an 84 SE, not a GT?  It has the WS6 package, and I've lowered the front.  Still seems to have the problem.  Could it also be I still have the original Eagle GT tires on it???  (it has only just over 50k miles on it)  Or Is it that I'm just used to it, and other cars are much worse to drive, and I just wouldn't know?||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||08-13-2001||03:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>...<BR>Could it also be I still have the original Eagle GT tires on it???  (it has only just over 50k miles on it)  Or Is it that I'm just used to it, and other cars are much worse to drive, and I just wouldn't know?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Original, as in 17 years old? If so, get some new tires and you should see a significant improvement. Tires harden with age, regardless of the miles. Performance tires will help even more but practically any new tire should give you an improvement.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||08-13-2001||03:31 PM||||Back to the original question: Yes, I saw pics of a Grand Am type dash in a Fiero- it wasn't a kit, but something someone modified to put in there. Unfortunately I have no clue where the pics are, but hey I guess that means that somehow it's possible.<P>Oh and Jonathan, not all Fieros handle *quite* as well as yours, it's not quite stock if ya hadn't noticed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||08-13-2001||07:22 PM||||I posed the question recently about other dashboard/interior stuff that would be fit into Fieros. I was thinking of trying something like that as well. Someone mentioned early 90s F-bodies. The only thing I can think of that might be a problem is the angle which the bottom of the dash goes to the floor. In the GPs, GAs, and F-bodies, they take a long dip downward. You need something that turns back sharply in a Fiero.<P>I'm still thinking of taking measurements and maybe trying something, but more likely will just build something custom.<P>Let us know if you have any luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
